{
 "id": "e2-xi-chain-1",
 "description": "Synthetic survey-drone registry. Four registry names for what may be one drone are linked in a chain d1=d2, d2=d3, d3=d4 by the system. Claims about fleet membership are stated under different names: the system asserts d4 and d2 are members of fleet-north; a harbour office denies d1 is a member (accepted by the system). After the mark before-denial, an auditor denies that d1 and d4 are the same (accepted by the system), so the established group {d1, d2, d3, d4} then contains a denied pair. A second perspective, fleet-desk, accepts the system's links and the two membership assertions, and nothing from the harbour office or the auditor. Same-as claims carry no valid interval (identity is timeless content, v0.2 3.4).",
